  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: 7 refill requests from 3 patients.\n\n- pt-0027 Frank Odum, lisinopril 10 mg: not refilled. I first renewed it (mr-t0001) because the 8/27 outside potassium of 5.9 was hemolyzed, and ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0002). Then an outside BMP from 10/20 arrived with a valid potassium of 5.8, so I cancelled the renewal before it was dispensed. Urgent review task to Dr. Okafor (task-t0019), corrected message to the patient, note written. sr-t0002 is still open.\n- pt-0030 Samuel Price:\n  - Metformin 1000 mg twice daily: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004). Three requests (one portal, two pharmacy) were handled as one. eGFR is 58 after correction and HbA1c was 7.1% on 8/19.\n  - Lisinopril 20 mg: not refilled. I first renewed it (mr-t0003). Then the lab corrected the 10/06 creatinine to 1.49, a 35% rise over 1.10 within 4 weeks of the dose increase, so I cancelled the renewal before it was dispensed. Urgent review task to Dr. Okafor (task-t0020), corrected message to the patient, note written.\n- pt-0031 Marcus Webb:\n  - Lisinopril 10 mg: 30-day supply with no refills (mr-t0005), and a BMP ordered (sr-t0006). The last BMP was collected 10/20/2025, just over 12 months ago, and he had a visit on 9/28/2026.\n  - Metformin 500 mg twice daily: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). The 10/14 eGFR of 39 was entered in error; the valid eGFR is 92 and HbA1c was 6.9% on 9/28.\n  - A potassium of 4.6 drawn on its own (10/22) arrived later. It is not a BMP, so the decision stands.\n\nEach patient got a reply. All message items are closed.\n\n- Lisinopril status: for Mr. Odum and Mr. Price, the earlier prescriptions were stopped when I placed the renewals and stay stopped now that the renewals are cancelled. Neither currently has an active lisinopril prescription.\n- Still open: I left the results-queue items open, including those that arrived during this session (inbox-a0001, a0002, a0004) and older results like critical potassiums for pt-0016 and pt-0008. They are outside this request.",
